<title>USA: EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 05-FEB.</title>
<headline>EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 05-FEB.</headline>
<text>
<p>Tropical Cyclone Pancho-Helinda, with 40 mph winds, is in the southern Indian Ocean near 20s/85e, moving southwest at 7 mph. It is expected to move southwestward through 48 hours then turn more to the south again, when it should be dissipating. The threat to shipping continues moderate at this time but will lessen with time.</p>
</text>
